{
  "meta": {
    "title": "Clone your voice, locally",
    "source": {
      "kind": "repo",
      "url": "https://github.com/garvitkhurana/mlx-voice-clone"
    },
    "fps": 30,
    "size": [
      1920,
      1080
    ],
    "voice": {
      "backend": "say",
      "voice": "Samantha",
      "rate_wpm": 175
    },
    "glossary": [
      {
        "term": "TTS",
        "plain": "voice model"
      },
      {
        "term": "transcript",
        "plain": "exactly what you said"
      }
    ]
  },
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "title",
      "type": "title",
      "duration_s": 3,
      "narration": [
        "MLX voice clone reads any script aloud, in your own voice."
      ],
      "data": {
        "title": "mlx-voice-clone",
        "subtitle": "Clone your voice, locally",
        "kicker": "No cloud service · no per-use bill · just your Mac"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "idea",
      "type": "flow",
      "duration_s": 4,
      "narration": [
        "Record a short clip of your voice.",
        "Add a script: the words you want said.",
        "A voice model, Qwen three TTS, takes both, on your Mac.",
        "Out comes your script as narration, in your voice. No cloud, no per-use bill."
      ],
      "data": {
        "title": "A short clip of your voice + a script = narration",
        "roles": {
          "input": "neutral",
          "model": "c2",
          "output": "c3"
        },
        "nodes": [
          {
            "id": "clip",
            "label": "Voice clip",
            "role": "input",
            "art": "wave"
          },
          {
            "id": "script",
            "label": "Script",
            "role": "input",
            "art": "lines"
          },
          {
            "id": "model",
            "label": "Qwen3 TTS",
            "sub": "on your Mac",
            "role": "model",
            "shape": "trapezoid"
          },
          {
            "id": "out",
            "label": "Narration",
            "sub": "in your voice",
            "role": "output",
            "art": "wave"
          }
        ],
        "edges": [
          {
            "from": "clip",
            "to": "model"
          },
          {
            "from": "script",
            "to": "model"
          },
          {
            "from": "model",
            "to": "out"
          }
        ],
        "steps": [
          {
            "id": "clip",
            "do": "reveal",
            "targets": [
              "clip"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "script",
            "do": "reveal",
            "targets": [
              "script"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "learn",
            "do": "flow",
            "path": [
              "clip",
              "model"
            ],
            "kind": "request"
          },
          {
            "id": "read",
            "do": "flow",
            "path": [
              "script",
              "model"
            ],
            "kind": "request"
          },
          {
            "id": "out",
            "do": "flow",
            "path": [
              "model",
              "out"
            ],
            "kind": "response"
          }
        ],
        "beats": {
          "clip": 0,
          "script": 1,
          "learn": [
            2,
            0.0
          ],
          "read": [
            2,
            0.35
          ],
          "out": 3
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "local",
      "type": "compare",
      "duration_s": 4,
      "narration": [
        "Why run it locally?",
        "It runs on your Mac, after one model download.",
        "There's no bill per use.",
        "And your clip and script stay local."
      ],
      "data": {
        "title": "Why local",
        "left": {
          "label": "Your Mac",
          "role": "c3"
        },
        "right": {
          "label": "Cloud service",
          "role": "neutral"
        },
        "rows": [
          {
            "left": "Runs on your Mac",
            "right": "Runs on remote servers"
          },
          {
            "left": "No per-use bill",
            "right": "Often billed per use"
          },
          {
            "left": "Clip and script stay local",
            "right": "Clip and script are uploaded"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "generate",
      "type": "steps",
      "duration_s": 8,
      "narration": [
        "Here's what happens when you hit generate.",
        "First, your clip is converted to a standard format, and cached.",
        "The voice model loads once, and is reused for every piece.",
        "Your script is split into pieces, at paragraphs and sentences.",
        "Each piece is spoken in your voice.",
        "And the pieces are stitched into one audio file."
      ],
      "data": {
        "title": "What happens when you hit generate",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": "Prepare your clip",
            "sub": "converted once, then cached",
            "code": [
              "\"\"\"Return path to 24kHz mono WAV,",
              "    converting with ffmpeg if needed."
            ]
          },
          {
            "label": "Load the model once",
            "sub": "reused for every piece",
            "code": [
              "# Load once so chunked runs",
              "loaded_model = load_model(model_id)"
            ]
          },
          {
            "label": "Split the script",
            "sub": "at paragraphs and sentences",
            "code": [
              "chunks = _split_long_text(",
              "    text, max_chars=cc)"
            ]
          },
          {
            "label": "Speak each piece",
            "sub": "in your voice, one pass each",
            "art": "wave",
            "code": [
              "for i, chunk in enumerate(chunks, start=1):",
              "    _run(",
              "        model=loaded_model,",
              "        text=chunk,",
              "        ref_audio=ref_wav,"
            ]
          },
          {
            "label": "Stitch into one file",
            "sub": "joined end to end",
            "code": [
              "path = _concat_wavs(part_paths, merged)",
              "\"\"\"Concatenate WAV parts losslessly",
              "via ffmpeg concat demuxer.\"\"\""
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "pieces",
      "type": "chunks",
      "duration_s": 6,
      "narration": [
        "Why pieces? In one pass, the model would cut a long script short.",
        "So the script is split into pieces, each under a size limit.",
        "Each piece gets its own pass through the model.",
        "Then the pieces are joined end to end, into one file."
      ],
      "data": {
        "title": "Long scripts are made in pieces, then stitched",
        "doc": "your script",
        "chunks": [
          4,
          3,
          3
        ],
        "engine": {
          "label": "Qwen3 TTS",
          "sub": "one pass per piece"
        },
        "output": "one .m4a file"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "two_ways",
      "type": "alternatives",
      "duration_s": 4,
      "narration": [
        "Two ways in, one engine.",
        "The command line is one command, easy to rerun or automate.",
        "The browser page runs that same command, and shows progress as it goes."
      ],
      "data": {
        "title": "Two ways in, one engine",
        "panels": [
          {
            "label": "Terminal",
            "kind": "terminal",
            "role": "c4",
            "lines": [
              {
                "cmd": "uv run python scripts/qwen3_clone.py"
              },
              {
                "comment": "plus your clip, your script, lite or pro"
              },
              {
                "out": "Saved narration"
              }
            ],
            "caption": "batches & automation"
          },
          {
            "label": "Voice clone",
            "kind": "browser",
            "role": "c4",
            "url": "127.0.0.1:8765",
            "fields": [
              {
                "label": "Script",
                "value": "Hey! I'm Garvit Khurana…"
              },
              {
                "label": "Quality",
                "value": "lite"
              }
            ],
            "slider": {
              "label": "Speed",
              "value": 0.6
            },
            "button": "Generate",
            "log": [
              "Loading model...",
              "Generating piece...",
              "Saved narration"
            ],
            "caption": "same engine, live progress"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "quality",
      "type": "metrics",
      "duration_s": 4,
      "narration": [
        "Lite is the faster model, for drafts while you iterate.",
        "Pro is bigger, for when the wording is final.",
        "And you can make it speak a little faster or slower."
      ],
      "data": {
        "cards": [
          {
            "label": "Lite",
            "value": "Drafts",
            "compare": "faster, while you iterate"
          },
          {
            "label": "Pro",
            "value": "Final takes",
            "compare": "when quality matters"
          },
          {
            "label": "Speaking speed",
            "value": "Adjustable",
            "compare": "a little faster or slower"
          }
        ],
        "footnote": "Default: lite"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "commands",
      "duration_s": 4,
      "narration": [
        "Three commands to start.",
        "On an Apple Silicon Mac with ffmpeg, uv sync sets it up.",
        "Record your clip, reading the lines provided.",
        "Then start the browser page, on your machine."
      ],
      "data": {
        "title": "Get started",
        "lines": [
          {
            "cmd": "uv sync",
            "note": "install"
          },
          {
            "cmd": "./scripts/record_sample.sh",
            "note": "record your clip"
          },
          {
            "cmd": "uv run python scripts/tts_ui_server.py",
            "note": "open the browser page"
          }
        ],
        "footer": "http://127.0.0.1:8765/"
      }
    },
